beta-beryllene, P-3m1 relaxation at 27x27 k (2026-10-01)

b-Beryllene_k27_relax (job 44066) relaxed the 11x11 P-1 geometry at 27x27 k: the cell became hexagonal
(|a1| = 2.1669, |a2| = 2.1668 A, 120.005 deg; P-3m1 at symprec 1e-3) and E0 dropped by 4.5 meV per cell. The energy was
constant to 1e-7 eV over ionic steps 20-28; the run then stopped with ZBRENT (EDIFFG -1E-3 below the force noise).
Here the result is symmetrised (a = mean length, Be at (1/3, 2/3) and (2/3, 1/3), same buckling and centre) and relaxed
again with the same INCAR, so that VASP keeps D3d. The P-1 cell of b-Beryllene is a k-mesh artefact of the 11x11 run.

Downstream recomputation in this geometry (submitted 2026-10-01; each stage uses the INCAR/KPOINTS of the old beta
directory next to it, only POSCAR changed; 5.0 PDoS with ISTART = 0 because there is no 105x105 WAVECAR):
